// READ THIS BEFORE THE SCOPE NOTE BELOW. THIS FILE DOES NOT RUN ON THE REQUIRED GATE, AND THE
// REASON IS NO LONGER THE ONE THIS NOTE USED TO GIVE. It said the required floor DECLINES every
// ReadsLiveTree module (v2.workflow.required_floor DeclinedLiveTree). That arm was DELETED at the
// root of v2.workflow.required_floor, so the reason stated here was true when written and is stale;
// the declaration itself stays, truthfully -- compile_dag_diagnostic_census resolves its synthetic
// sources against the live checkout -- and live_tree_disposition now answers only affected-set
// eligibility.
//
// WHAT IS TRUE TODAY: this module's name matches no row of v2.workflow.required_floor
// required_gate_prefixes and no row of required_gate_authored_modules, so after the 2026-09-19
// nominal-roster ruling the required floor discovers it and dispositions every identity in it
// DeclinedOutsideRequiredGate. A required floor run's green is evidence only for what it PLANNED,
// and nothing here is planned, so every probe below is AUTHORED evidence -- green under a local
// gunbc run --claim-run and under changed-witness selection on a PR that edits it, and executing
// nowhere else. That is strictly weaker than enrolment, and the gap-analysis rows this file serves
// must say so in line. In this file of all files the distinction matters: a witness that cannot
// execute is exactly the defect these probes count, and it applies to them first.
//
// DISSOLVES when a required-gate selector admits this module -- the derived changed-population
// selection v2.workflow.required_floor names as required_gate_bankruptcy's restoration trigger, or
// a re-homing of a class onto an admitted prefix as the zero-field family took (see the note where
