data guarantee_floor_class_probe_scope_note: String = "WHAT THIS FILE IS. Five floor classes in docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md carried rungs established by a ONE-OFF hand execution of compile_dag_diagnostic_census on 2026-08-01 (four of them said NOT ENROLLED in their own Evidence cell; the parse-separator row cited a session's throwaway probe). A SIXTH class was authored here and REMOVED before merge: the v2.-module direct-call argument-type exemption, which gunbc#8902 landed on main as direct_call_argument_type_class while this change was in flight. One concept, one authority (gunbc.design_argument::single_authority) — that seam is theirs, this file carries no second name for it, and the gap-analysis row for it cites their rows. Nothing re-ran any of them, so each rung was honest about the day it was measured and silent about today -- the shape gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder meta-obligation 4 forbids. This file is the authorship: each of those measurements is written as a probe that reds if the compiler's behaviour changes in either direction. WHERE EACH ONE EXECUTES IS A SEPARATE FACT AND IS NOT UNIFORM -- this module is outside v2.workflow.required_floor required_gate_prefixes and required_gate_authored_modules, so the probes that remain here execute only locally and under changed-witness selection, while the record-completeness ZERO-FIELD family was re-homed onto the admitted test.claim.infer_ prefix at test.claim.infer_record_field_completeness_zero_field_witness and executes on every required floor run. An earlier cut of this sentence claimed required-floor execution for all of them; that was true of the DeclinedLiveTree deletion and false of the roster cut that followed it. Rows that remain holes are ExpectSilentAcceptanceHole (gunbc.guarantee_probe_corpus guarantee_probe_below_floor_hole_rows), not a count in this sentence: a hole that climbs is rewritten as ExpectBlockingRefusal and stays as a permanent regression control (gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder (dissolution on climb)) — floor_field_through_generics_hole_probe / floor_field_through_generics_type_variable_refuses is that climb. Do not read a remaining hole-probe green as a guarantee: it pins a DEFECT. PROBE ADEQUACY, per the operator-adopted 2026-08-01 mandate that every below-floor row carry closure AND shape evidence: each hole ships beside a control that DOES refuse on this same harness and this same run -- the monomorphic record for generic instantiation, the declared-record field access for field-through-generics, the doubled separator for the omitted one, so a zero on the hole is the compiler's silence and never the harness failing to reach the judgment. The exhaustiveness hole's adequacy control is not re-authored here: the coproduct-scrutinee arm is already enrolled and executing at test.claim.match_exhaustiveness_coproduct_witness w_missing_coproduct_arm_reports_one_non_exhaustive, on this same harness, and duplicating it would be a second authority for one fact."

// THE INSTRUMENT THAT PRODUCED EVERY NUMBER BELOW IS A LOCALLY BUILT gunbc, AND ITS VINTAGE WAS
// TESTED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. Because the gate does not admit this file (see above), CI never re-runs
// these probes; a single local binary is their ONLY execution evidence, so that binary is a
// variable, not a given. CROSS-CHECK, 2026-08-22: two independently built binaries roughly fifteen
// hours apart ran the same four probes — both silent holes and both refusing controls — and
// returned identical verdicts, PASS on all eight. The pairs stay DISCRIMINATING in both, which is
// what matters: a binary refusing everything or nothing would show as a control flipping, and
// neither did. So the verdicts are not an artifact of one build. NOT established: that any binary
// in this family agrees with the seed CI would use, because no required lane executes this file;
// that question dissolves with gate admission and not before.

// MEASURED 2026-08-22 on this harness, full dag + src/v2 pool, before these probes were authored —
// the numbers the rows below encode. generic-instantiation hole 0 rows; monomorphic control 1
// blocking TypeMismatch; generic green 0. field-through-generics hole 0 rows; declared-record
// control 1 blocking InternalError; green 0. exhaustiveness type-variable hole 0 rows. record
// completeness red 1 blocking MissingField; green 0. parse list separator hole 0 rows;
// doubled-separator control 1 blocking ParseError; green 0. THE InternalError ROW IS PINNED AS
// OBSERVED, NOT AS ENDORSED: a field access naming no declared field refuses, the property the
// control exists to establish, but under a class name that says nothing about what went wrong. That
// is its own diagnostic-quality defect, recorded here rather than laundered into a nicer-sounding
// assertion; improving the class reds this probe, the correct place for the conversation.

fn census_of(source: String) -> CompileDiagnosticCensus {
  compile_dag_diagnostic_census(source)
}

fn measured_v1_compile_harness_source() -> NonEmptyStr {
  fold_list(
    xs: v1_compile_harness_source_paths(),
    empty: "guarantee-floor-class-harness-source" as NonEmptyStr,
    cons: fn(acc, path) {
      let read = filesystem_read(path: path)
      concat(
        concat(concat(acc as String, "\n=== "), path as String),
        concat(" ===\n", read.content as String),
      ) as NonEmptyStr
    },
  )
}

fn witness_harness_revision(probe: GuaranteeProbeId) -> MeasurementRevision {
  let harness_source = measured_v1_compile_harness_source()
  match active_probe_row(probe: probe) {
    Present { value: row } =>
      v1_compile_harness_revision(
        probe: probe,
        expectation: row.expectation,
        harness_source: harness_source,
      )
    Absent =>
      v1_compile_harness_revision(
        probe: probe,
        expectation: ExpectBlockingRefusal { diagnostic_class: "witness-harness-row-absent" as NonEmptyStr },
        harness_source: harness_source,
      )
  }
}

fn total_row_count_is_zero(census: CompileDiagnosticCensus) -> Bool {
  match census {
    CensusObserved { rows: rows } => count(rows) == 0
    CensusNotRunnable { cause: _ } => false
  }
}

fn row_holds(probe: GuaranteeProbeId, source: String) -> Bool {
  match active_probe_row(probe: probe) {
    Present { value: row } => probe_row_expectation_holds(census: census_of(source: source), row: row)
    Absent => false
  }
}

fn silent_hole_holds(probe: GuaranteeProbeId, source: String) -> Bool {
  let census = census_of(source: source)
  match active_probe_row(probe: probe) {
    Present { value: row } =>
      probe_expectation_is_below_floor_hole(e: row.expectation)
        && probe_row_expectation_holds(census: census, row: row)
        && total_row_count_is_zero(census: census)
    Absent => false
  }
}

fn blocking_verdict(source: String, wanted: String, holds: fn(Int) -> Bool) -> CensusVerdict {
  census_verdict(census: blocking_class_census(source: source, wanted_class: wanted), holds: holds)
}

data generic_instantiation_hole_source: String = "module probe_floor_generic_inst\ntype Boxed<T> { inner: T }\nfn f() -> Boxed<Int> { Boxed { inner: \"not an int\" } }\n"
data generic_instantiation_monomorphic_source: String = "module probe_floor_generic_mono\ntype Plain { inner: Int }\nfn f() -> Plain { Plain { inner: \"not an int\" } }\n"
data generic_instantiation_green_source: String = "module probe_floor_generic_green\ntype Boxed<T> { inner: T }\nfn f() -> Boxed<Int> { Boxed { inner: 1 } }\n"

// FIELD-ACCESS-ON-GENERIC CENSUS (roadmap node floor-generic-field-constraint-wall,
// first_slice: "Re-run the class census and list the surviving sites"). A site is a compiled
// fixture whose base is generic (bare parameter, callback parameter, bare generic name, or the
// result of a generic call); population = the sites listed in floor_census_sites below, drawn
// from the field-through-generics probe sources of this module plus the closed-wall candidate
// shapes measured at the released pack. FABRICATED-RESIDUE is what the census hunts: a field-MISS
// site that yields zero blocking rows. Non-miss sites are labelled CLEAN, never FABRICATED, so
// green controls cannot inflate the residue count.
type FloorCensusRow {
  site: String,
  source: String,
  is_field_miss: Bool,
  planted: Bool,
}

data field_through_generics_hole_source: String = "module probe_floor_field_generic\nfn get_field<T>(t: T) -> Int { t.no_such_field }\n"
data field_through_generics_record_source: String = "module probe_floor_field_record\ntype Plain { inner: Int }\nfn f(p: Plain) -> Int { p.no_such_field }\n"
data field_through_generics_green_source: String = "module probe_floor_field_green\ntype Plain { inner: Int }\nfn f(p: Plain) -> Int { p.inner }\n"

data exhaustiveness_type_variable_hole_source: String = "module probe_floor_exh_tyvar\ntype Colour = Red | Blue\nfn pick<T>(t: T) -> Int { match t { Red => 1 } }\n"

data record_completeness_red_source: String = "module probe_floor_record_missing\ntype Pair { a: Int, b: Int }\nfn f() -> Pair { Pair { a: 1 } }\n"
data record_completeness_green_source: String = "module probe_floor_record_full\ntype Pair { a: Int, b: Int }\nfn f() -> Pair { Pair { a: 1, b: 2 } }\n"
// THE ZERO-FIELD FORMS OF THIS CLASS MOVED OUT, and this note is the pointer rather than a second
// copy of them. The four sources and five witnesses that measure an empty brace pair, a bare name
// and the sanctioned `discriminant` seam now live at
// `test.claim.infer_record_field_completeness_zero_field_witness`, whose module name matches
// the `test.claim.infer_` row of `v2.workflow.required_floor` `required_gate_prefixes` -- so they
// execute on the required floor, which this module does not. What remains here is the
// PARTIAL-OMISSION red and its green control.

data parse_list_separator_hole_source: String = "module probe_floor_list_sep\ntype Cell { n: Int }\nfn f() -> List<Cell> { [ Cell { n: 1 }, Cell { n: 2 }  Cell { n: 3 } ] }\n"
data parse_list_separator_double_source: String = "module probe_floor_list_sep_double\ntype Cell { n: Int }\nfn f() -> List<Cell> { [ Cell { n: 1 }, , Cell { n: 3 } ] }\n"
data parse_list_separator_green_source: String = "module probe_floor_list_sep_green\ntype Cell { n: Int }\nfn f() -> List<Cell> { [ Cell { n: 1 }, Cell { n: 2 }, Cell { n: 3 } ] }\n"

// CLIMBED: the type-argument hole is closed at b5af75f4d339 (gunbc#9416; red at its parent 107304a57920). The probe was
// `floor_generic_instantiation_is_still_silently_accepted`; per gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder (dissolution on
// climb) it is flipped to the refusal and stays enrolled as the permanent regression control for the higher rung.
// ASSERT-THEN-BYTES: the located refusal must be present with the pinned class AND the
// pinned subject; the row PASSES when it is (main's idiom, per review 17051 - a witness
// must not be green-when-broken). When it is missing, the failure reason renders every
// observed row, so the receipt bytes arrive exactly when a reader needs them. This
// replaces the six TEXT-CARRIER rows, which failed by design and inverted the polarity
// of the wall they certified.
// ONE COMPILE PER ASSERTED SOURCE (review 17051 round-3 non-blocking point): the located
// refusal is asserted AND its bytes rendered from a single total_rows_census. The hit
// filter and the census classifier share census_blocking_rows, so "refused" means
// BLOCKING in both instruments by construction. On a miss the reason carries every
// observed row - the receipt bytes arrive exactly when a reader needs them.
fn located_refusal_assert(source: String, wanted_class: String, wanted_subject: String) -> CensusVerdict {
  match total_rows_census(source: source) {
    CensusObserved { rows: rows } => {
      let hits = count(filter(census_blocking_rows(rows: rows), f: fn(r) { (r.diagnostic_class as String) == wanted_class && r.subject_name == wanted_subject }))
      if hits >= 1 {
        CensusHeld {}
      } else {
        CensusDisagreed { reason: concat("located refusal missing: ", concat(wanted_class, concat("|", concat(wanted_subject, "| observed: ", fold(rows, init: "", f: fn(acc, r) { concat(acc, concat(concat(concat((r.diagnostic_class as String), "|"), r.subject_name), concat("|", concat(census_int_text(n: r.count), ";")))) }))))) }
      }
    }
    CensusNotRunnable { cause: cause } => CensusUnobserved { cause: cause }
  }
}

// DEFERRED-BASE legs (roadmap node floor-generic-field-constraint-wall). Measured at main with
// main's released binaries (CI release-bins pack, run 45457628228, head 6e4f2148767): the located
// refusals below are the OBSERVED outcomes, not assertions of intent; the shape once enrolled as
// a silent-acceptance hole (generic-result base) has CLIMBED - it now refuses with a located
// cause - and is dissolved to ExpectBlockingRefusal per guarantee_ladder.md, kept as a permanent
// regression control. Every refusal source has a licensed twin differing only in the field
// existing or the result type being concrete, so a refusal cannot be attributed to the fixture.
data floor_census_src_rec_generic_field: String = "module probe_floor_census_rec_generic\ntype R<T> { v: T }\nfn f<T>(r: R<T>) -> Int { r.v.no_such_field }\n"
data floor_census_src_chain_inner: String = "module probe_floor_census_chain\ntype Boxed<T> { inner: T }\nfn f<T>(x: Boxed<T>) -> Int { x.inner.no_such_field }\n"
data floor_census_src_conc_result: String = "module probe_floor_census_conc_result\ntype Boxed<T> { inner: T }\nfn mk<T>(v: T) -> Boxed<T> { Boxed { inner: v } }\nfn g() -> Int { mk(v: 5).no_such_field }\n"
data floor_census_src_conc_result_green: String = "module probe_floor_census_conc_result_green\ntype Boxed<T> { inner: T }\nfn mk<T>(v: T) -> Boxed<T> { Boxed { inner: v } }\nfn g() -> Int { mk(v: 5).inner }\n"
data floor_census_src_nested_generic: String = "module probe_floor_census_nested\ntype Boxed<T> { inner: T }\ntype Wrap<T> { w: Boxed<T> }\nfn f<T>(z: Wrap<T>) -> Int { z.w.inner.no_such_field }\n"

// Census population: 13 field-access-on-generic sites. The planted positive control is
// main-bare-T-parameter-read (would fabricate without the #11285 wall).
data floor_census_sites: List<FloorCensusRow> = [
  FloorCensusRow { site: "main-bare-T-parameter-read", source: field_through_generics_hole_source, is_field_miss: true, planted: true },
  FloorCensusRow { site: "main-declared-record-control", source: field_through_generics_record_source, is_field_miss: true, planted: false },
  FloorCensusRow { site: "main-concrete-receiver-green", source: field_through_generics_green_source, is_field_miss: false, planted: false },
  FloorCensusRow { site: "deferral-lambda-param", source: field_through_generics_deferral_lambda_param_source, is_field_miss: true, planted: false },
  FloorCensusRow { site: "deferral-lambda-param-twin", source: field_through_generics_deferral_lambda_param_green_source, is_field_miss: false, planted: false },
  FloorCensusRow { site: "deferral-bare-generic-name", source: field_through_generics_deferral_generic_result_source, is_field_miss: true, planted: false },
  FloorCensusRow { site: "deferral-generic-result-base", source: field_through_generics_deferral_generic_result_hole_source, is_field_miss: true, planted: false },
  FloorCensusRow { site: "deferral-generic-result-base-twin", source: field_through_generics_deferral_generic_result_hole_green_source, is_field_miss: false, planted: false },
  FloorCensusRow { site: "closed-wall-generic-record-field", source: floor_census_src_rec_generic_field, is_field_miss: true, planted: false },
  FloorCensusRow { site: "closed-wall-chained-inner", source: floor_census_src_chain_inner, is_field_miss: true, planted: false },
  FloorCensusRow { site: "closed-wall-concrete-boxed-result", source: floor_census_src_conc_result, is_field_miss: true, planted: false },
  FloorCensusRow { site: "closed-wall-concrete-boxed-result-green", source: floor_census_src_conc_result_green, is_field_miss: false, planted: false },
  FloorCensusRow { site: "closed-wall-nested-generic", source: floor_census_src_nested_generic, is_field_miss: true, planted: false },
]

// THE STATUS IS KEYED ON BLOCKING ROWS (review 17051 round 3): total_rows_census is
// "THE WHOLE CENSUS, blocking filter NOT applied", so counting it would let a
// warning-only acceptance of a field-miss render as BLOCKED - the exact fabrication the
// census hunts. A field-miss site is FABRICATED-RESIDUE unless at least one BLOCKING row
// refuses it; twins are CLEAN when nothing blocks them. The rendered count is
// blocking/total, so advisory noise stays visible without ever becoming a verdict.
// Each site compiles EXACTLY ONCE per test: premises read the single rendered string.
fn floor_census_status_for(rows: List<CompileDiagnosticCensusRow>, is_field_miss: Bool) -> String {
  let n = count(census_blocking_rows(rows: rows))
  if n == 0 { if is_field_miss { "FABRICATED-RESIDUE" } else { "CLEAN" } } else { "BLOCKED" }
}

fn floor_census_render_row(row: FloorCensusRow) -> String {
  match total_rows_census(source: row.source) {
    CensusObserved { rows: rows } => {
      let n = count(census_blocking_rows(rows: rows))
      let t = count(rows)
      concat(row.site, concat(":", concat(floor_census_status_for(rows: rows, is_field_miss: row.is_field_miss), concat(":", concat(census_int_text(n: n), concat("/", census_int_text(n: t)))))))
    }
    CensusNotRunnable { cause: cause } => concat(row.site, concat(":NOT-RUNNABLE:", cause))
  }
}

// MEASURED FIXTURE (main pack, gunbc sha 6707d9c4...): the callback receiver is an
// INSTANTIATED generic record (Boxed { inner: 5 } with T inferred from the field value),
// so the refusal below is a field-miss on a properly instantiated generic, keyed by the
// real base label. The earlier fixture passed x: 1 (T = Int) and its twin read .inner on
// Int - neither expressed field-access-on-generic; both were replaced 2026-11-25 after
// review 17051.
data field_through_generics_deferral_lambda_param_source: String = "module probe_floor_field_deferral_lambda_v2\ntype Boxed<T> { inner: T }\nfn apply2<T, R>(x: T, k: Int, f: fn(T, Int) -> R) -> R { f(x, k) }\nfn g() -> Int { apply2(x: Boxed { inner: 5 }, k: 0, f: (x_a, k_a) => x_a.no_such_field) }\n"
// ACCEPTED POSITIVE CONTROL: same shape reading the field that EXISTS on the
// instantiated base (Boxed<Int>); measured RC=0 with the released pack (gunbc sha
// 6707d9c4...), with exactly one ADVISORY row (EffectSummaryIncompleteAtFunctionValue at
// apply2 - an effect-summary lower bound, not a refusal), so the census can tell
// zero-because-clean from zero-because-blind on this shape: zero BLOCKING rows.
data field_through_generics_deferral_lambda_param_green_source: String = "module probe_floor_field_deferral_lambda_green_v2\ntype Boxed<T> { inner: T }\nfn apply2<T, R>(x: T, k: Int, f: fn(T, Int) -> R) -> R { f(x, k) }\nfn g() -> Int { apply2(x: Boxed { inner: 5 }, k: 0, f: (x_a, k_a) => x_a.inner) }\n"
data field_through_generics_deferral_generic_result_source: String = "module probe_floor_field_deferral_result\ntype Boxed<T> { inner: T }\nfn g() -> Int { Boxed.no_such_field }\n"
// RE-LABELLED 2026-11-25 after #17051 review. The earlier string wrote the record
// literal with EXPLICIT type arguments (Boxed<Int> { inner: 5 }) inside an expression -
// a form the released grammar does not accept as a record literal: it parses as the
// comparison chain Boxed < Int > {...}, whose value really is Bool, so the observed
// "no field ... on type 'Bool'" was a refusal of a MIS-PARSED program, not of a generic
// field read. `Boxed<Int> { inner: 5 }` in a let-position parse-fails outright (measured).
// The true generic-call-result shape uses the inferred literal; measured at the main
// pack this fixture refuses "no field 'no_such_field' on type 'Boxed'" - the real
// instantiated base label, not a fabricated one.
data field_through_generics_deferral_generic_result_hole_source: String = "module probe_floor_field_deferral_result_hole_v2\ntype Boxed<T> { inner: T }\nfn inj<T>(v: T) -> T { v }\nfn g() -> Int { inj(v: Boxed { inner: 5 }).no_such_field }\n"
// ACCEPTED POSITIVE CONTROL (measured RC=0, main pack): the same call reading the
// field that EXISTS on the instantiated result is a valid program and the compiler
// accepts it. This is the rung-honesty positive control for the class: the refusal above
// is discriminating because this accepted control sits beside it.
data field_through_generics_deferral_generic_result_hole_green_source: String = "module probe_floor_field_deferral_result_hole_twin_v2\ntype Boxed<T> { inner: T }\nfn inj<T>(v: T) -> T { v }\nfn g() -> Int { inj(v: Boxed { inner: 5 }).inner }\n"


test fn floor_generic_instantiation_type_argument_refuses() -> ProcessExit {
  census_verdict_all([
    census_premise("the probe row's expectation holds", row_holds(probe: floor_generic_instantiation_hole_probe, source: generic_instantiation_hole_source)),
    blocking_verdict(source: generic_instantiation_hole_source, wanted: "TypeMismatch", holds: fn(n) { n == 1 })
  ])
}

test fn floor_generic_instantiation_monomorphic_control_refuses() -> ProcessExit {
  census_verdict_all([
    census_premise("the probe row's expectation holds", row_holds(probe: floor_generic_instantiation_monomorphic_control_probe, source: generic_instantiation_monomorphic_source)),
